	(text "J1 is the CP-A cable socket, dual-in-line numbering. Pins 1 to 8 are D0 to D7. Pins 9 to 16 are open: on the CP-A they are already tied to pins 1 to 8, so grounding them would short the data bits. J2 plugs onto bus-master J5. Odd pins are D0 to D7. Even pins are left open here; J5 already grounds them. Solder the dual-in-line socket on the front and the 2x8 socket on the back."
		(at 25 145 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
		(uuid "9b0ca5c4-5a0d-48b2-9e98-ef622a875e07")
	)
